  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-ip-nullspace-property": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $m,n\\in\\mathbb N$ with $m,n\\ge1$, and let\n$A\\in M_{m\\times n}(\\mathbb R)=\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$.\nPut $[m]:=\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ and $[n]:=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$. The library indexes\nvector coordinates and matrix columns by $n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ and matrix rows\nby $m=\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$. Throughout this item use the canonical relabeling\n$j\\mapsto j-1$ from $[n]$ to the library's coordinate and column indices, and\nsimilarly from $[m]$ for rows. Thus write\n$u_j:=u(j-1)$ and $A_{ij}:=A(i-1,j-1)$. For $u\\in\\mathbb R^n$, define\nthe matrix-vector product by\n$$(Au)_i:=\\sum_{j=1}^n A_{ij}u_j \\qquad (i\\in[m]),$$\nand define\n$$\\ker A:=\\{h\\in\\mathbb R^n:Ah=0\\}.$$\nFor $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$ and $S\\subseteq[n]$, let $h_S\\in\\mathbb R^n$ be the\nvector whose $j$th coordinate is $h_j$ for $j\\in S$ and $0$ for $j\\notin S$;\nwrite $S^c:=[n]\\setminus S$. For $u\\in\\mathbb R^n$, write\n$$\\|u\\|_1:=\\sum_{j=1}^n|u_j|,$$\nthe same $p=1$ norm as the library's finite-dimensional norm under this\ncoordinate relabeling.\nFor $s\\in\\mathbb N$ with $1\\le s\\le n$, the matrix $A$ satisfies the **strict\nnullspace property of order $s$** if\n$$\\|h_S\\|_1<\\|h_{S^c}\\|_1$$\nfor every nonzero $h\\in\\ker A$ and every $S\\subseteq[n]$ with $|S|\\le s$.\nThis condition concerns exact kernel vectors only and says nothing about vectors\nwith $Ah\\ne0$."
    ],
    "thm-ip-basis-pursuit-exact-recovery-under-nsp": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $m,n,s\\in\\mathbb N$ with $m,n\\ge1$ and $1\\le s\\le n$, and let\n$A\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$ satisfy the strict nullspace property of order\n$s$. Use one-based coordinate labels $j=1,\\ldots,n$, with coordinate $j$\nidentified with the library's coordinate $j-1$. If $x^\\dagger\\in\\mathbb R^n$\nhas at most $s$ nonzero coordinates, then\n$x^\\dagger$ is the unique minimizer of\n$$\\sum_{j=1}^n|z_j|$$\nover all $z\\in\\mathbb R^n$ satisfying $Az=Ax^\\dagger$. This is a noiseless\nexact-data result; it makes no exact-recovery or support-recovery assertion for\nnoisy observations."
    ],
    "lem-ip-nullspace-property-stability-cone": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $m,n,s\\in\\mathbb N$ with $m,n\\ge1$ and $1\\le s\\le n$, and let\n$A\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$. Use one-based coordinate labels\n$j=1,\\ldots,n$, with coordinate $j$ identified with the library's coordinate\n$j-1$. Assume that\n$$\\sum_{j\\in S}|h_j|<\\sum_{j\\notin S}|h_j|$$\nfor every nonzero $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$ with $Ah=0$ and every\n$S\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ with $|S|\\le s$. Then there is a constant\n$\\rho\\in(0,1)$ such that\n$$\\sum_{j\\in S}|h_j|\\le\\rho\\sum_{j\\notin S}|h_j|$$\nfor every $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$ with $Ah=0$ and every\n$S\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ with $|S|\\le s$. The estimate is only on the exact\nkernel and gives no bound for vectors with $Ah\\ne0$."
    ],
